sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser (Next.js web)
    participant N as nginx (/api/ → api:3000)
    participant C as AuthController
    participant S as AuthService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant AG as AccessTokenGuard
    participant TG as TenantGuard
    participant RG as RolesGuard
    participant PG as PermissionGuard
    participant AC as AcademicScopeService
    participant M as Feature Service

    B->>N: POST /auth/login {email, password} (Origin checked)
    N->>C: forward
    C->>S: login(email, password)
    S->>DB: SELECT users WHERE email = normalized
    DB-->>S: user row (status active, passwordHash)
    S->>S: bcrypt.compare
    S->>DB: INSERT auth_sessions (refreshTokenHash SHA-256, expiresAt)
    S-->>C: { user, accessToken {sub,sid}, refreshToken, csrfToken }
    C-->>B: 200 + Set-Cookie x3 (httpOnly access_token, httpOnly refresh_token path=/api/v1/auth, csrf_token)

    alt Authenticated tenant request (e.g. GET /content)
        B->>N: GET /content + Cookie + x-institute-id + (x-csrf-token on writes)
        Note over AG,PG: Guard chain: AccessToken → Tenant → Roles → Permission
        AG->>DB: verify JWT (HS256, 15 min) + session row live + user status active
        DB-->>AG: session + user status
        AG-->>C: request.user = { userId }
        TG->>DB: getMembership(userId, x-institute-id, membership + institute active)
        DB-->>TG: membership + roles
        TG-->>C: request.tenant = { instituteId, membershipId, roles }
        RG->>RG: @RequiredRoles against tenant.roles (OR, optional)
        PG->>DB: grantKeysForMembership (permissions DB-fresh, never from JWT)
        DB-->>PG: granted keys (manage implies action)
        PG->>AC: resolveScope(membershipId)
        AC-->>PG: whole-institute (admin) or subject-set
        C->>M: service call scoped by tenant.instituteId
        M->>DB: queries filtered by institute_id + academic scope predicate
        DB-->>M: rows (tenant + scope scoped)
        M-->>C: response
        C-->>B: 200 JSON
    end

    opt Refresh rotation
        B->>C: POST /auth/refresh (refresh_token + CSRF, repair-only CSRF)
        C->>S: verify refresh token → session lookup
        S->>S: strict one-time rotation (no grace window), lineage on reuse
        S->>DB: UPDATE revoked_at = now() WHERE id = ? AND revoked_at IS NULL
        S->>DB: INSERT successor session (rotated_from_sid)
        C-->>B: rotated access + refresh cookies
    end